    "memoText": " \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 130\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 1780-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to incentivize the purchase of local produce in supermarkets\n      and grocery stores through the FreshConnect program\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  would expand the FreshConnect program by providing certain\npeople with two dollars in rebates to be used for the purchase of  addi-\ntional  local  produce for every two dollars of local produce purchased,\nincluding local produce sold in supermarkets and grocery stores.\n \n  Currently, the FreshConnect program is used  at  farmers'  markets  or\nfarm  stands  to  make  buying  fresh,  local food from our farmers more\naccessible.   I also recently announced the  launch  of  a  new  digital\nFreshConnect  initiative  to provide eligible New Yorkers with a digital\noption to buy SNAP-eligible farm products at  the  farmers'  market  and\nstreamline  the redemption process for New York farmers participating in\nthe program.  However, this bill would lead to  significant  operational\nissues  for  the  State and would require significant resources from the\nDepartment of Agriculture and Markets that are not accounted for in  the\nState's financial plan.\n \n  Therefore, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
